            <!-- <image width="45%" source="images/tandem-sphere-V-t"><description><p>ADD ALT TEXT TO THIS IMAGE</p></description></image> -->
<!--          </figure> -->
        </sidebyside>
        </answer>
      <solution>
        <p>Since water is removed at a constant rate, <m>V = 36\pi - 1.2t</m>. The approximate values are: <m>t = 0, V \approx 113.1</m>; <m>t = 20, V \approx 89.1</m>; <m>t = 40, V \approx 65.1</m>; <m>t = 60, V \approx 41.1</m>; <m>t = 80, V \approx 17.1</m>; <m>t = 94.24, V \approx 0</m>. The graph is linear because water is removed at a constant rate.</p>
          <sidebyside width="50%" valign="middle">
